  "chapter": 526,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 11 Chapter 526\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 3567-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to\n        permitting the sale or promotional gifting of certain complemen-\n        tary products for wine and spirits\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill authorizes the sale  or  inclusion  of  certain  promotional\nitems  with the purchase of an alcoholic beverage product. This practice\nenables manufacturers to effectively market and sell their products.\n \n  This bill as written, however, would only allow a wholesaler to trans-\nport and sell these products to a retailer. It would not  authorize  the\nretailer to, in turn, sell those products to the consumer. Additionally,\na consumer should continue to have the option to purchase a single prod-\nuct  without  the  promotional  items  and not be required to purchase a\npackaged, promotional set as the only  way  to  purchase  the  alcoholic\nbeverage  product.  I  have reached an agreement with the Legislature to\naddress these concerns in the upcoming legislative session. On the basis\nof that agreement, I am signing this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2023
 },
